# UI skill routing (MIS)

Three design skills are installed globally under `~/.agents/skills/`. They are **manual-only** (`disable-model-invocation: true`). Do not load more than one in the same turn.

## Which to use

| Need | Skill | How to invoke |
|------|--------|----------------|
| New marketing/landing page (e.g. Solar) with distinctive art direction | `design-taste-frontend` | User types `/design-taste-frontend` or asks for Taste Skill |
| Design system first: style, palette, fonts, UX checklist | `ui-ux-pro-max` | User types `/ui-ux-pro-max` |
| Critique / audit / polish an existing page | `impeccable` | User types `/impeccable` |

## Sequence for a new section (recommended)

1. `/ui-ux-pro-max` — pick system (optional but good for Solar energy look)
2. `/design-taste-frontend` — build the page
3. `/impeccable` — audit and polish

## If the user does not name a skill

Ask which of the three to use, using the table above. Do not invent a parallel design brief that conflicts with an already-chosen skill.

## Stack note

This project is Next.js (pages router) with existing Motion/`motion` usage. Prefer that stack; do not switch to GSAP/Three.js unless the user asks.
